<DocsLayout title="Editor" description="Core editor behavior in Axon">
  <h1>Editor</h1>

  <p>
    Axon's editor is built for daily project work: open files, keep multiple
    panes active, preview Markdown and media, and protect dirty changes before a
    tab closes. Recent stabilization work also focused on preserving scroll
    position, avoiding editor flicker, and keeping Monaco state owned by the
    active editor instead of remounting surfaces unnecessarily.
  </p>

  <figure class="docs-image">
    <img src="/media/screenshots/axon-screenshot-01.png" alt="Axon editor workspace with the file tree and empty editor state" loading="lazy" />
    <figcaption>The main Axon workbench keeps the file tree, editor area, status bar, and workspace context visible before you open a file.</figcaption>
  </figure>

  <h2>Tabs and panes</h2>
  <p>
    Files open into editor tabs. Tabs can be moved between panes, pinned, and
    closed with dirty-file prompts when unsaved changes exist.
  </p>

  <h2>Previews</h2>
  <p>
    Markdown, images, videos, and HTML can open in preview surfaces. External
    links use the system browser, while local Markdown links stay inside Axon
    when the target file exists in the workspace.
  </p>

  <h2>Find in file</h2>
  <p>
    Use the editor find control for current-file search. Selected text seeds
    the query when opening find, and editing the find query does not steal the
    original editor cursor after a query already exists. Workspace search is
    separate and opens results at the matching line and column.
  </p>

  <h2>Editor stability</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Dirty saves preserve the current scroll position instead of jumping to the bottom of the file.</li>
    <li>Change decorations are replaced instead of stacked, so repeated edits do not deepen yellow, green, or red paint.</li>
    <li>Command/control-click is treated as the explicit jump-to-definition gesture for imported and exported symbols.</li>
    <li>TypeScript hover rendering avoids competing stacked hover cards for the same symbol.</li>
    <li>Embedded HTML in TSX/JSX receives themed token colors instead of falling back to plain white text.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Deleted files</h2>
  <p>
    If a file is deleted from disk while it is still open, Axon marks the tab so
    you can see the editor no longer points at an existing file.
  </p>
</DocsLayout>
